{"name":"Sheepskin Gloves","hex":"#ad9e87","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sheepskin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The skin of a sheep, especially an adult sheep, and especially when used to make parchment or in bookbinding.","The tanned skin of a sheep with the fleece left on, especially when used for clothing, rugs, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheepskin"},{"term":"gloves","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of glove"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of glove"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gloves"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sheepskin","blocks":[{"text":"Sheepskin is the hide of a sheep, sometimes also called lambskin. Unlike common leather, sheepskin is tanned with the fleece intact, as in a pelt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Sheep_skin_for_sale.jpg/330px-Sheep_skin_for_sale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheepskin","wikidata":"Q1083901"},{"title":"Glove","blocks":[{"text":"A glove is a garment covering the hand, with separate sheaths or openings for each finger including the thumb. Gloves protect and comfort hands against cold or heat, damage by friction, abrasion or chemicals, and disease; or in turn to provide a guard for what a bare hand should not touch."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG/330px-Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glove","wikidata":"Q169031"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/SuperUgg.JPG/500px-SuperUgg.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse